```c
(*chain)[*chain_len - 1] = (*extra_certs)[i];  // move to chain
(*extra_certs)[i] = (*extra_certs)[i];  // self-assign
(*extra_certs_len)--;  // now _extra_certs_len points to element i, which is still the same pointer
```

Wait, after `(*extra_certs_len)--`, the valid elements of `_extra_certs` are `[0, *extra_certs_len-1]`. If `i == old_len - 1`, then after decrement, `*extra_certs_len == old_len - 1 == i`. So the valid elements are `[0, i-1]`. Element `i` is no longer counted. So the cert at element `i` is only in `_chain`. No double-free.

